teps performed during the first phase satisfies\nL180@P1: EN [Ld] ∼ EN [Md] ∼\nL181@P1: d + 1\nL182@P1: Ed\nL183@P1: · log N\nL184@P1: and involves the entropy Ed of the underlying Brun dy\u0002namical system in dimension d.\nL185@P1: When d → ∞, the entropy Ed satisfies Ed ∼ log d.\nL186@P1: The number Rd of steps performed during the remain\u0002der of the execution (after the first phase) has a mean\nL187@P1: value that is asymptotic to a constant rd.\nL188@P1: (b) Let Od be the number of quotients equal to 1 during the\nL189@P1: first phase. The ratio between the means EN [Od] and\n"
